Description:

JMAP fixes for spec compliance found by the JMAP-TestSuite.  Changes a
client can see:

CalendarEvent/get computes utcStart/utcEnd of floating events in Etc/UTC
unless the new timeZone argument names another zone; it used the
calendar's time zone.  Setting utcStart on a floating event now gives it
the calendar's timeZone (or Etc/UTC), on update as well as create, and
reports it.  utcEnd alone on a floating event reads its start in Etc/UTC.

CalendarEvent/set rejects a recurrenceOverrides patch on @type, method,
organizerCalendarAddress, participants/*/calendarAddress, privacy,
prodId, recurrenceId, recurrenceIdTimeZone, sentBy, uid,
recurrenceOverrides or recurrenceRule with invalidProperties, as
jscalendarbis requires; these were ignored.  relatedTo can now be patched.
utcStart with start, utcEnd with duration, and either inside an override
are rejected too.  An override written over CalDAV that gives a
participant another address reads back with that attendee as a separate
participant.

Calendar/set and AddressBook/set reject an empty name.

ContactCard/set rejects a photo that is not an image, and members on a
card whose kind is not "group".

Blob/lookup returns unknownDataType for a type whose capability is not
in "using".  Blob/get accepts a length of 0.

EmailSubmission/set returns invalidProperties for an unknown emailId,
not "emailNotFound", and noRecipients for an empty rcptTo.

The fallback Identity of a user without a domain uses
userid@defaultdomain as its email, not "".  MDN/send and SieveScript/test
use the same address, and so now prefer defaultdomain to servername.


